From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 17:50:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ARM64EC: print the lines of the first 256 exceptions, then
 count them by kind

Every exception through ResetToConsistentState printed five to seven
lines (the exception, the context reconstruction, the guest rip, pass
through or rethrow), and Wine and the Mach handler add theirs. World of
Warcraft's x64 client takes an execute fault per 4 KB page of its code
(about 3,300 pages to its login screen under desktop Wine), and run
20261101T172555 looped on one: its log passed the 256 MiB dev cap and
the run could not be measured.

The lines of the first 256 exceptions print as before. After that each
is counted, by kind (access violation read, write or execute,
breakpoint, single step, illegal instruction, misalignment, other) and
outcome (passed through, rethrown to the guest, handled here), and an
[exc-census] line gives the counts every 65536 exceptions and at most
every 5 s (CNTVCT_EL0) while they keep coming. The tracker's
[iOS-xrem] via=protect line, one per protection change that removes
execute, prints for the first 64 and every 4096th, with the count.

Linear: PLA-516
Class: diagnostics
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-11-01-wow-x64-fex.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 Source/Windows/ARM64EC/Module.cpp             | 111 ++++++++++++++++--
 Source/Windows/Common/InvalidationTracker.cpp |  12 +-
 2 files changed, 112 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Source/Windows/ARM64EC/Module.cpp b/Source/Windows/ARM64EC/Module.cpp
index 10e382a..b6b4a0e 100644
--- a/Source/Windows/ARM64EC/Module.cpp
+++ b/Source/Windows/ARM64EC/Module.cpp
@@ -588,6 +588,80 @@ void HandleImageUnmap(uint64_t Address, uint64_t Size) {
